snippet.textDisplay:
@Sam-w5v The World Hunger Index is an international organization based in Germany, not in China. The data used is also not the self-reported ones, but rather sourced through United Nations organizations, like UNICEF, World Bank, WHO and etc.

Also Chinese state media accurately reported back in 1995 and 1996 that their first 2 attempted spaceflight launches Apstar 2 and Intelsat 708 blew up and killed a combined 12 people. Are you sure they lie about all statistics? If so, why would they not cover this up?

I'll be honest, I think, on a purely pragmatic level, it's in China's best interests to make sure their massive population stays alive as much as possible. They need every important advantage to continue their rise in the world leaderboards. I believe it's the same reason why China spent the last decade finding other countries to source massive amounts of soybeans from in the event of a US-China trade war. Previously, China got most of their soybeans from the US, however China mitigated most of the pain through their prior preparations.

